messages:
john_c: Hey team, streaming SSE from our Next/Vite app to Redwood API hangs on first chunk in prod. Works locally. Anyone seen this?

alex: sorry to hear — can you paste the snippet you're using and SDK + node versions? Also is this deployed to Vercel edge runtime or server (Node)?

john_c: Using Vercel edge runtime (export const runtime = 'edge'). Code:

```ts
import Redwood from 'redwood-inference';

const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY, streaming: true });

export default async function handler(req) {
  const res = await client.generate({ model: 'gptx', prompt: 'stream test' });
  return new Response(res.body, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' } });
}
```

node: 18.16.0
npm: 9.6.7
sdk: "redwood-inference": "^2.2.0"

maria: curious — local vs prod difference usually means runtime or proxy: does Vercel strip Authorization header or alter streaming behavior? any logs?

john_c: No obvious errors. On client side the SSE connection opens then nothing. Server logs show request -> 200 but no chunk logs. Repro steps: curl from local to prod endpoint returns 200 and content-type but body never starts.

jit: can you try a direct curl with -N and --http2? sometimes proxies buffer until connection completes.

john_c: ran `curl -v --http2 -N https://our-app.vercel.app/api/stream` -> shows handshake then connection idle.

alex: two likely causes: 1) SDK is using Node streams vs WHATWG ReadableStream in older SDKs which can hang in edge runtimes, 2) Authorization header removed by edge middleware or Next config. What does `res.body` type resolve to in your handler? try logging `typeof res.body` and `res.body?.getReader`.

john_c: logged: `typeof res.body = object` and `res.body.getReader = undefined` (so no getReader).

maria: that matches: ++ older SDK returns a Node Readable (object) which in edge runtime doesn't implement getReader.

alex: quick workaround: in your handler convert Node stream to a web ReadableStream using web-streams-polyfill or the SDK helper. But polyfills can be heavy and may not run in true edge environments. Long term fix: upgrade SDK.

john_c: what's the exact upgrade + changelog? we can't change runtime easily on this release.

alex: The SDK 2.3.0+ includes a streaming path that returns a WHATWG ReadableStream when `runtime: 'edge'` is detected and falls back otherwise. Recommend upgrading to 2.4.0 which also fixes a bug where auth headers were dropped for proxied streaming requests.

jit: if you can't upgrade immediately, try this minimal shim in the handler (if Vercel supports it):

```ts
import { Readable } from 'stream';
import { ReadableStream as WebReadable } from 'web-streams-polyfill/ponyfill';

function nodeToWeb(nodeStream) {
  return new WebReadable({
    start(controller) {
      nodeStream.on('data', (chunk) => controller.enqueue(chunk));
      nodeStream.on('end', () => controller.close());
      nodeStream.on('error', (err) => controller.error(err));
    }
  });
}

const webStream = nodeToWeb(res.body);
return new Response(webStream, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' } });
```

alex: also check that Vercel isn't removing Authorization: on edge functions some integrations need `fetch(req, { headers: req.headers })` or forwarding explicitly. Try logging headers at the platform edge.

john_c: tried the shim locally and on prod (added polyfill to package). Locally it worked. On prod the polyfill failed with "ReferenceError: globalThis.WebAssembly is not defined" — looks like true edge environment blocks that polyfill.

maria: yep polyfills often fail on edge. Upgrading is safer. If you upgrade to 2.4.0, the client uses WHATWG streams and should just return a Response-ready body. Also 2.4.0 respects X-Accel-Buffering and chunking headers.

john_c: ok upgrading now...

(20m pass)

john_c: upgraded to "redwood-inference@2.4.0" and redeployed — streaming now starts immediately and chunks flow. 🎉

alex: awesome. Can you paste the final logs showing chunk lines so we can close the ticket?

john_c: paste logs:

```
[INFO] /api/stream request start
[STREAM] chunk 0: "data: {\"id\":1,\"text\":\"hello\"}\n\n"
[STREAM] chunk 1: "data: {\"id\":2,\"text\":\"world\"}\n\n"
[INFO] /api/stream request end
```

alex: thanks — filing a follow-up: SDK: add clearer error message when returned body is Node stream in edge runtime, and support-diagnostics: guide for polyfills and header forwarding.

support-bot: Ticket #SUP-12987 created for SDK streaming-edge followups.

maria: note for ops — we should add a telemetry event when client returns a stream without getReader in edge-configured requests.

john_c: thanks team, saved our release. :tada:
